sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch07-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The brood-parasitic instinct of the European cuckoo was generated by natural selection from an ancestor that built its own nest but occasionally laid eggs in other birds’ nests, where the fostered young fared better.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cuckoo brood parasitism evolved from occasional laying in other birds’ nests";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter VII, “Instinct”; section “Natural instincts of the cuckoo, ostrich, and parasitic bees”. Scope: cuckoos and other brood-parasitic birds"
}
